  "derived_judgments": [
    "A subprocess is function-like for reuse only relative to an explicit or trusted environment closure; value-shaped RPC arguments do not establish purity.",
    "Anneal should classify effects by semantic input, execution policy, observation, and authority-changing state rather than placing every side effect in one undifferentiated shell.",
    "Persistent workers are optimizations over an effect-control contract, not a semantic model by themselves.",
    "A general effect system may strengthen in-process host APIs but cannot replace runtime mediation, isolation, or trust accounting for opaque foreign execution."
  ]
